==============================================================================
6. Answer
==============================================================================
optimum (continuous eta): eta = 0.958, vf = 0.60
  density 0.6561 g/cm^3, E(HP-MT) 3514.9 MPa, E(HP-DS) 3517.1 MPa
  HS feasibility: target is below the HS upper bound (10729.5 MPa at the stiffest corner) -> not bound-violating; the HP-MT estimate lies inside its own HS band.
nearest catalogue grade: S32 at vf = 0.60 -> rho 0.6640 g/cm^3, E 3610.6 MPa

Caveat: HP-MT/HP-DS are idealised estimates (perfect bonding, no matrix porosity, no particle breakage); experimental syntactic-foam moduli typically fall 20-40 % below HP-MT, so the design should carry margin above the 3500 MPa target.
